{
  "_comment": [
    "Filter definitions for transform.sh — consumed as: .filters[] | filterKey|downloadUrl|version",
    "Source: https://github.com/hagezi/dns-blocklists (adblock/ = AdGuard syntax, ||domain^).",
    "hagezi publishes no hosts-format directory, so transform.sh converts ||domain^ -> 0.0.0.0 domain.",
    "version is null on purpose: transform.sh reads the real '! Version:' line from each downloaded file.",
    "To drop a list, delete its object. To add one, copy an object and change name/filterKey.",
    "Deliberately EXCLUDED — these do not work as DNS hosts entries:",
    "  *-ips.txt (doh-ips, nameserver-ips, tif-ips): contain ||1.2.3.4^ -> would emit '0.0.0.0 1.2.3.4'.",
    "      Use these in /ip/firewall address-list instead, not /ip/dns/adlist.",
    "  whitelist-*.txt and spam-tlds-adblock-allow.txt: allow rules (@@||domain^), not blocklists.",
    "  spam-tlds*.txt: bare TLDs (||actor^) -> '0.0.0.0 actor' matches only that literal hostname,",
    "      not *.actor, so it blocks nothing. TLD blocking needs regex rules, not an adlist."
  ],
